    <div class="effective">Effective Date: April 8, 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="/">www.theaiad.studio</a></div>

    <h2>1. Purpose</h2>
    <p>This Moderation Policy governs the use of <em>The AI Ad Studio</em> platform ("the Platform"), which enables users to create digital advertising content using artificial intelligence tools.</p>
    <p>Our goal is to ensure that all generated content is safe, lawful, ethical, and aligned with our platform values.</p>

    <hr class="divider">

    <h2>2. Prohibited Content</h2>
    <p>The following types of content are strictly forbidden on the Platform under any circumstances:</p>

    <div class="warning-box">
      <p>Violations of this policy may result in immediate account suspension and reporting to relevant authorities where required by law.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>2.1 Exploitation &amp; Sexual Content</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Child exploitation or any content involving minors in a sexualized context</li>
      <li>Pornography or explicit sexual material</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.2 Violence &amp; Harm</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Depictions of violence against people or animals</li>
      <li>Content that endorses, glorifies, or incites physical harm</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.3 Hate &amp; Harassment</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Hate speech, discrimination, or harassment</li>
      <li>Content targeting individuals or groups based on race, religion, gender identity, age, nationality, sexual orientation, disability, or any protected characteristic</li>
      <li>Threats or incitement to violence or harassment</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.4 Illegal Activities</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Promotion, facilitation, or endorsement of illegal or unlawful activities, including drug use or trafficking, hacking or cybersecurity violations, and fraud or criminal acts</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.5 Misinformation &amp; Manipulation</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Spreading misinformation or disinformation</li>
      <li>Promotion of conspiracy theories intended to mislead or manipulate</li>
      <li>False or misleading advertising claims</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.6 Privacy Violations</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Sharing or generating private, personal, or confidential information without proper consent</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.7 Regulated Advice</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Unauthorized or unverified legal, medical, or financial advice</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.8 Political Content</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Political campaigning</li>
      <li>Direct lobbying or targeted political persuasion</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.9 Fraud &amp; Deception</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Scams, spam, or deceptive practices</li>
      <li>Impersonation or misleading representation</li>
      <li>Intellectual property violations, including unauthorized use of copyrighted material, trademarks, or likenesses</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.10 Platform Discretion</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Any other content deemed inappropriate, harmful, or contrary to the values and standards of The AI Ad Studio</li>
    </ul>

    <hr class="divider">

    <h2>3. User Responsibilities</h2>
    <p>By using the Platform, users agree to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Comply with this Moderation Policy at all times</li>
      <li>Ensure that prompts, inputs, and generated outputs adhere to applicable laws and ethical standards</li>
      <li>Take responsibility for all content created, edited, or published via the Platform</li>
    </ul>

    <hr class="divider">

    <h2>4. Moderation Process</h2>
    <p>To maintain a safe and compliant environment, The AI Ad Studio employs a multi-layered moderation system:</p>

    <h3>4.1 Automatic Screening</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>AI-driven systems scan prompts and generated content in real time</li>
      <li>Detection includes keywords, image recognition, and behavioral signals</li>
      <li>Content may be blocked, flagged, or restricted automatically</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>4.2 Manual Review</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Human moderators review flagged or borderline content</li>
      <li>Additional contextual analysis is applied to ensure fair decisions</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>4.3 User Reporting</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Users can report content they believe violates this policy</li>
      <li>Reports are prioritized and reviewed promptly</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>4.4 Enforcement Actions</h3>
    <p>Violations may result in one or more of the following actions:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Content removal or blocking</li>
      <li>Warnings or temporary restrictions</li>
      <li>Suspension or permanent account termination</li>
      <li>Reporting to relevant authorities where required by law</li>
    </ul>

    <hr class="divider">

    <h2>5. Policy Updates</h2>
    <p>This Moderation Policy will be updated periodically to reflect the introduction of new AI tools and capabilities, changes in legal and regulatory requirements, evolving risks related to AI-generated content, and improvements in prompt handling and content generation processes.</p>
    <p>Users are responsible for reviewing the latest version of this policy. Continued use of the Platform constitutes acceptance of any updates.</p>

    <hr class="divider">

    <h2>6. Enforcement &amp; Compliance</h2>
    <p>The AI Ad Studio reserves the right to interpret and enforce this policy at its sole discretion, take immediate action to prevent harm or legal risk, and refuse service to users who violate or attempt to circumvent safeguards.</p>

    <hr class="divider">

